WEBVTT

00:00:00.194 --> 00:00:03.340
Round-robin routing sends requests to backends in turn.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.140
It is simple and can work when servers and requests are similar.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.980
Local LLM environments often are not that uniform.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.330
One server may have a stronger GPU, another may have a smaller model,

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.036
and a third may already be busy with long-context work.

00:00:15.036 --> 00:00:18.339
Round-robin is easy to start with, but it is not capacity awareness.

00:00:18.339 --> 00:00:22.400
Least-connections routing sends new work toward the backend with fewer active connections

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.070
or requests.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.035
That can be better than round-robin, but it still needs caution.

00:00:26.035 --> 00:00:29.193
One long generation can consume more resources than several short calls.

00:00:29.193 --> 00:00:32.890
A streaming client may hold a connection open while tokens arrive slowly.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.700
Connection count is a signal, not a complete performance model.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.340
Weighted routing lets stronger or lighter-loaded backends receive more traffic.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.640
Health-check-based routing prevents traffic from going to servers that are down,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.560
still loading a model, repeatedly failing, or not ready for the requested workload.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.280
Good health checks are more than checking whether a port is open;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.195
they should reflect whether the backend can actually serve the request.

00:00:52.195 --> 00:00:56.885
More mature setups add model-aware routing, endpoint-aware routing, queues, failover,

00:00:56.885 --> 00:00:59.097
request timeouts, retry policies, and backpressure.

00:00:59.097 --> 00:01:03.575
Model-aware routing confirms that the requested model or capability exists on a backend.

00:01:03.575 --> 00:01:07.315
Backpressure tells clients the service is busy instead of allowing slow failure.

00:01:07.315 --> 00:01:12.000
The routing strategy should reflect real capacity, model availability, and workload type.
